  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="29">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 29</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="29">[Not in D]</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="29" corresp="#wit-k">⁊ la understande man georne þæt eal swylc is to leanne ⁊ næfre to lufianne.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">And now behold it must be clearly understood that all such are to be censured and not to be indulged in.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und traun, man begreife ernstlich, dass all solches zu verschmähen und niemals zu pflegen ist.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And indeed, let it be earnestly understood that all such things are to be rejected and never cherished.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Only in K.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
